From ab9c94cd603485067db9196248be95e544b0cd1f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:55:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/12] feat(capture): add SCStream-based single-frame capture
 for macOS 13

SCScreenshotManager is macOS 14+ and was the only ScreenCaptureKit call in
ScreenCaptureClient that blocks the Ventura backport. Route both capture
paths through SingleFrameCapturer, which uses SCScreenshotManager where
available and otherwise VenturaSingleFrameCapture: a short-lived SCStream
that waits for the first `.complete` frame, converts it via a shared
CIContext, and stops. Idle-only content (common on Ventura for static
screens) is accepted after 15 frames / 1.5 s, and a 3 s timeout throws
the new ScreenCaptureError.captureTimedOut. Filters, configuration math
(sourceRect in points, width/height in pixels) and own-window exclusion
are unchanged.

displayLocalRect now takes the screen frame instead of an NSScreen so the
AppKit-to-SCK flip is covered by ScreenCaptureGeometryTests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015SN3yT97jK8sWhBx4KgSJn
