From 7c93f1d09d03080946b201b6a6c8906ab9ecd9ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 12:57:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] feat(ocr): add macOS 13 Ventura recognition pipeline
 beside the macOS 26 one
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Split OCRClient into a thin dispatching client plus shared pure helpers,
and move the existing RecognizeDocumentsRequest implementation unchanged
into ModernOCRPipeline (@available macOS 26). liveValue now picks
ModernOCRPipeline on macOS 26 and VenturaOCRPipeline everywhere older.

VenturaOCRPipeline runs the classic VNRecognizeTextRequest (revision 3,
accurate, language correction, auto-detect or a validated BCP-47 code)
through ClassicVisionTextRecognizer, which executes the blocking handler
on a detached task and keeps the non-Sendable observations there.
VenturaOCRLayout infers what the document API no longer provides —
paragraph groups, alignment, and vertical CJK columns — from geometry and
script, and is pure so it can be unit-tested without Vision.

VisionWarmUp is now pipeline-agnostic (the caller supplies the probe
requests) so both paths share the same in-flight serialization.
JapaneseRubyOCRCorrector uses the classic API on every OS; scoring and
slot mapping are unchanged.

