From a8747146f31c22d9b5f15f745d472d18f3312894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 13:02:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] feat(translation): add provider abstraction with Google
 Cloud Translation for macOS 13
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Apple Translation's `TranslationSession(installedSource:target:)` is macOS 26,
so the Ventura backport needs another backend. Introduce a `TranslationProvider`
protocol and move the existing session logic verbatim into
`AppleTranslationProvider` (`@available(macOS 26.0, *)`, including the 26.4
strategy/styled path). Add `GoogleCloudTranslationProvider` (Cloud Translation
v2 over URLSession: JSON body, key in `X-Goog-Api-Key`, ≤128-segment /
≤28k-char chunks translated concurrently, one retry on 429/5xx, cancellation
mapped to `CancellationError`, `/languages` listing cached per key and
persisted, curated static list including Arabic when no key is stored).

`TranslationClient` becomes a thin shell that picks the provider from the new
`translation.provider` setting (default `.apple` on 26+, `.google` below) and
keeps all shared post-processing (id matching, label extraction, newline
capping, stall watchdog). API keys live in the Keychain behind
`TranslationCredentialClient`. Settings gains a provider picker and a secure
API-key field; `TranslationModelHint` explains the missing key and opens the
app's Settings when Google is the backend. `Language.systemSupported` no longer
imports Translation and intersects with `VNRecognizeTextRequest`, which exists
on every supported release.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
