Subject: [PATCH 05/12] backport: macOS 13 availability shims, Perception
 tracking, and Ventura CI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Compile-time availability fixes for the macOS 13.0 deployment target:

- Sources/Compat/CompatGlass.swift: `compatGlass(_:in:)` (Liquid Glass on
  macOS 26, ultraThinMaterial + hairline border + optional tint below) and
  `compatProminentButtonStyle()` (.glassProminent / .borderedProminent).
  Replaces all 8 `.glassEffect` sites and the `.glassProminent` button.
- Sources/Compat/CompatWindowDrag.swift: `compatWindowDrag()` — SwiftUI
  `WindowDragGesture` on macOS 15+, an NSViewRepresentable calling
  `NSWindow.performDrag(with:)` before that. Overlay hit-zone logic untouched.
- OverlayWindowModel: `@Observable` -> `@Perceptible` (swift-perception);
  `Perception` added as an explicit app dependency (Project.swift +
  Tuist/Package.swift, same pinned version).
- `WithPerceptionTracking` wraps every view body that reads TCA
  `@ObservableState`, `@Shared` or the perceptible overlay model.
- AppFeature: `Observations { }` (macOS 26) -> swift-sharing `Shared.publisher`
  + `removeDuplicates()`, applying the current value first.
- `count(where:)` / trailing-closure `count { }` (Swift 6 stdlib, macOS 15
  runtime) -> `.filter { }.count` at all 11 sites; `preferCountWhere`
  SwiftFormat rule disabled so it isn't reintroduced.
- `AccessibilitySettings.prefersHorizontalTextLayout` (+ notification) guarded
  behind macOS 15; `false` / never-firing publisher before that.
- `ContentUnavailableView` (14) gets a VStack fallback; `.rect` shape
  shorthands (14) -> concrete shapes; two-parameter `onChange` (14) ->
  single-value form.

CI: .github/workflows/build.yml ("Build (Ventura backport)") builds Release
Universal 2 at MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET=13.0, runs tests, verifies lipo
archs / vtool minos / LSMinimumSystemVersion, and uploads the zipped app and
logs. .mise.toml notes that tuist should be pinned after the first run.
docs/VENTURA-BACKPORT.md documents the compatibility layer.

